<title>SPAIN: Spain's Rato says budget to prompt rate decline.</title>
<headline>Spain's Rato says budget to prompt rate decline.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Friday he anticipated lower interest rates based on the budget.  </p>
<p>Speaking to journalists after a cabinet meeting, Rato said &quot;If the budget policy does its job -  which is to come up with a budget that fulfills the criteria of the European Union for the single currency - then we must surely be in a position of less inflationary tension, and therefore of lower rates.&quot;</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
